📘 DevOps Linux + SSH Cheat Sheet (PDF Ready)
🧠 SYSTEM INFORMATION
uname -a              → Kernel & system info
cat /etc/os-release   → OS details
whoami                → current user
id                    → user + groups

📂 FILE & DIRECTORY

ls -la        → list all files
pwd           → current directory
cd /path      → change directory
mkdir folder  → create folder
rm file       → delete file
rm -rf folder → force delete folder

📄 FILE VIEWING (LOGS IMPORTANT)
cat file        → show full file
less file       → scroll file
head file       → first lines
tail file       → last lines
tail -f file    → live logs (VERY IMPORTANT)

⚙️ PROCESS MANAGEMENT
ps aux        → all processes
top           → live system usage
htop          → better view (if installed)
kill -9 PID   → force kill process

🌐 NETWORKING
ping google.com     → check connectivity
curl URL            → fetch request
wget URL            → download file
ss -tulnp           → open ports
lsof -i :8080       → check port usage

📦 PACKAGE MANAGEMENT (Ubuntu)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install package
sudo apt remove package

🔐 SSH (VERY IMPORTANT)
ssh user@ip
ssh -i key.pem user@ip
ssh-keygen -t ed25519
ssh-copy-id user@ip

🔐 SSH FILE LOCATIONS
~/.ssh/id_rsa              → private key
~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub          → public key
~/.ssh/authorized_keys     → server allowed keys

🔐 PERMISSIONS
chmod 777 file   → full access (danger)
chmod 755 file   → standard apps
chmod 700 file   → owner only
chmod 600 file   → secure file
chown user:group file → change owner

💾 DISK & MEMORY
df -h       → disk usage
du -sh dir  → folder size
free -m     → RAM usage

📜 LOGS
tail -f /var/log/syslog   → live logs
journalctl -u service     → service logs
dmesg | tail              → system logs

⚙️ SERVICES (systemctl)
systemctl status nginx
systemctl start nginx
systemctl stop nginx
systemctl restart nginx

🐳 DOCKER (DEVOPS CORE)
docker ps
docker images
docker run -it ubuntu
docker exec -it container bash
docker logs container_id

🧪 DEBUG FLOW (REAL DEVOPS)
1. Check logs
2. Check processes
3. Check ports
4. Check disk
5. Check services

